  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine how many ounces of milk James has left, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Convert the total amount of milk from gallons to ounces.\n2. Subtract the amount of milk James drank from the total amount of milk.\n\nFirst, we know that there are 128 ounces in a gallon. James has 3 gallons of milk, so we calculate the total amount of milk in ounces as follows:\n\\[ 3 \\text{ gallons} \\times 128 \\text{ ounces/gallon} = 384 \\text{ ounces} \\]\n\nNext, we subtract the 13 ounces that James drank from the total amount of milk:\n\\[ 384 \\text{ ounces} - 13 \\text{ ounces} = 371 \\text{ ounces} \\]\n\nTherefore, the amount of milk James has left is \\(\\boxed{371}\\).",
